From: Grokbot <grokbot@s-w.art>
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: vivobook-s15: camera power-on settle (Phase C)

Live 7.2.2-13: ov02c10 binds 8-0036 (CCI1 i2c1 @ 0x36 is correct).
rpmh accepts vreg_l2m/l4m/l7m voltage sets, then:

  ov02c10 8-0036: Error reading reg 0x300a: -110
  ov02c10 8-0036: failed to find sensor: -110

After fail the three vregs are present but disabled (num_users=0).
That is ov02c10_power_off() on the identify_module error path --
NOT proof that pm8010-m is a no-op. CMD-DB has ldom2/4/7.

ov02c10_power_on() order (do not patch the driver):
  1) clk_prepare_enable (MCLK)
  2) regulator_bulk_enable (dovdd, avdd, dvdd)
  3) reset assert 2 ms, deassert, wait 5 ms
  4) CCI read 0x300a
No gpio237/gpio100/MCLK dmesg is expected unless those get/enable
calls fail. Clock get already succeeded (else "imaging clock").

This DTS iteration:
  * startup-delay-us = 10 ms on the wired LDOs so bulk_enable
    returns after a settle window (driver only waits 5 ms after
    reset). Not regulator-always-on / boot-on -- last resort only.
  * Declare unused l1m/l3m so a later one-line supply swap is
    possible if these LDOs are the wrong physical rails.
  * Do not enable OV08X40 (same 0x36). FHD+IR spec and OF bind
    at 8-0036 still point at OV02C10; -110 is no-ACK not chip-id
    mismatch.

Signed-off-by: Grokbot <grokbot@s-w.art>
